16:T502,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":"The Complete Guide to Daily Namaz Rakats: Step-by-Step Breakdown for Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha","description":"Complete authentic guide to daily namaz rakat counts for Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha. Includes Fard, Sunnah, Nafl, and Witr prayer breakdown.","image":["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1591604129939-f1efa4d9f7fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"],"datePublished":"2026-10-15T08:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-10-15T08:00:00Z","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Sheikh Tariq Al-Madani & Editorial Board","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/about"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Namaz-e-Shariq","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/web-app-manifest-512x512.png"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog/complete-guide-daily-namaz-rakats"},"keywords":"namaz rakat, namaz ki rakat, namaz rakat table, rakat namaz, rakat in namaz, zuhar namaz rakat, asr namaz rakat, namaz ke faraiz, namaz with urdu translation, tasbeeh namaz, namaz janaza, janaza namaz dua, tarabi namaz, shabe baraat namaz, shab e barat ki namaz ki niyat, beter namaz porar niyom, namaz chadar, namaz e ghufayla"}17:T59c,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How many total obligatory (Fard) rakats are there each day?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There are 17 obligatory (Fard) rakats performed throughout the day: 2 for Fajr, 4 for Dhuhr, 4 for Asr, 3 for Maghrib, and 4 for Isha."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between Sunnah Mu’akkadah and Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sunnah Mu’akkadah refers to prayers that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) persistently performed and rarely abandoned; missing them deliberately without valid reason is strongly disapproved. Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah refers to voluntary Sunnah prayers that carry immense reward when performed, but leaving them does not incur blame."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many rakats are in Isha prayer?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The complete Isha prayer consists of 17 rakats: 4 Sunnah (Ghayr Mu’akkadah), 4 Fard, 2 Sunnah (Mu’akkadah), 2 Nafl, 3 Witr Wajib, and 2 Nafl."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Witr obligatory in the Hanafi school?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the Hanafi school of jurisprudence, Witr is categorized as Wajib (necessary/incumbent), meaning missing it requires Qada (making up). In the Shafi’i, Maliki, and Hanbali schools, Witr is classified as Sunnah Mu’akkadah."}}]}c:["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950 min-h-screen py-10 transition-colors duration-200","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$16"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Articles\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"The Complete Guide to Daily Namaz Rakats: Step-by-Step Breakdown for Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha\",\"item\":\"https://namaz-e-shariq.com/blog/complete-guide-daily-namaz-rakats\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$17"}}],"$L18"]}]
