23:["$","$L28",null,{"items":[{"question":"How many total obligatory (Fard) rakats are there each day?","answer":"There are 17 obligatory (Fard) rakats performed throughout the day: 2 for Fajr, 4 for Dhuhr, 4 for Asr, 3 for Maghrib, and 4 for Isha."},{"question":"What is the difference between Sunnah Mu’akkadah and Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah?","answer":"Sunnah Mu’akkadah refers to prayers that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) persistently performed and rarely abandoned; missing them deliberately without valid reason is strongly disapproved. Sunnah Ghayr Mu’akkadah refers to voluntary Sunnah prayers that carry immense reward when performed, but leaving them does not incur blame."},{"question":"How many rakats are in Isha prayer?","answer":"The complete Isha prayer consists of 17 rakats: 4 Sunnah (Ghayr Mu’akkadah), 4 Fard, 2 Sunnah (Mu’akkadah), 2 Nafl, 3 Witr Wajib, and 2 Nafl."},{"question":"Is Witr obligatory in the Hanafi school?","answer":"In the Hanafi school of jurisprudence, Witr is categorized as Wajib (necessary/incumbent), meaning missing it requires Qada (making up). In the Shafi’i, Maliki, and Hanbali schools, Witr is classified as Sunnah Mu’akkadah."}],"title":"Key Questions & Rulings Answered"}]
